        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-07T15:51:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We tend to play mostly random where we are - or what feels like fun.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Or if we are looking for a specific type of game, we'll cherry pick. The Randomizer on spiffs website (spifworld.com/sotm) is great for that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But you are correct. Rook City is regarded as one of the hardest environments in the game at the moment. &nbsp;It's great that you are playing them Thematically, but part of the wonder of the game is that you can mix and match so many different variables that you can create an endless stream of games. You &nbsp;might consider playing in Insulis Primalis or Tomb of Anubis just to get the hang of the Chairman (I consider those the most friendly (hah!) environments, from my experience) and then return to the story aspect that you have going on when you have a better feeling of how he works.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
